## Executive Summary

GPT-5.5 Pro is OpenAI's high-capability model optimized for deep reasoning and accuracy on complex, high-stakes workloads, released April 23, 2026 (ChatGPT) and April 24, 2026 (API). It features a massive 1.05M token context window, premium pricing ($30/$180 per 1M tokens), and exceptional performance on multi-tool orchestration benchmarks (90.1% on BrowseComp, highest among GPT-5.5 family). The model is designed for long-horizon problem solving, agentic coding, and precise execution across multi-step workflows. GPT-5.5 Pro leads the GPT-5.5 family on BrowseComp (90.1% vs 84.4% for GPT-5.5) and achieves 28.3 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index (86th percentile). It costs 6x more than GPT-5.5 ($30/$180 vs $5/$30) but offers higher accuracy for complex tasks. Independent testing shows GPT-5.5 Pro delivers equal or better results than GPT-5.5 for complex workflows, with some users noting the cost is not justified for most use cases.

